    "field": "Walker circulation change",
    "problem": "Current climate models struggle to reproduce the observed intensification of the Walker circulation over the last three decades, likely due to their inability to accurately simulate decadal variations in El Ni\u00f1o patterns and their response to natural variability.",
    "method": "This study uses Empirical Orthogonal Function (EOF) analysis on multiple observational datasets of atmospheric and oceanic variables to identify coherent decadal trends, which are then attributed to the increased frequency of central Pacific-type El Ni\u00f1o events to explain the intensified Walker circulation.",
    "task": "The task is to examine observational evidence of an intensified Walker circulation over the past three decades (1979-2008) and contrast these findings with results from general circulation models which deviate from the observed trend.",
