            "target_entity_instance": "brightness temperature (TB)",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "In order to relate changes in the UTH to convective activities over the warm pool region, we use three-decade-long NOAA HIRS channel brightness temperature (TB) around the 6.7-\u00b5m water vapor absorption band (Shi and Bates 2011), in which the channel's weighting function is around the 200-500 hPa layer.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "El Ni\u00f1o",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "tropical Indian and Pacific Oceans",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The first EOF mode of the SST, contributing 40.4 % of the total variance over 30 years (1979\u20132008) over the tropical Indian and Pacific Oceans, depicts the well-known El Ni\u00f1o/La Ni\u00f1a pattern (Fig. 1a).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "El Ni\u00f1o",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "equatorial eastern Pacific",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "By combining the vector loadings with the associated PC time series, one can find distinct positive SST anomalies over the equatorial eastern Pacific and horseshoe-like cold anomalies sur rounding the warm anomaly regions during El Ni\u00f1o years such as 1982-1983, 1987-1988, and 1997\u20131998.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "La Ni\u00f1a",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "eastern Pacific",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "During La Ni\u00f1a years, very low SST anomalies over the eastern Pacific and high SST anomalies over the western Pacific are noted.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "La Ni\u00f1a",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "western Pacific",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "During La Ni\u00f1a years, very low SST anomalies over the eastern Pacific and high SST anomalies over the western Pacific are noted.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "El Ni\u00f1o/Southern Oscillation (ENSO)",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "western tropical Pacific",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The EOF mode 1 of SLP, explaining 21.7% of the total variance, shows an east-west separated pattern in the vector loading (Fig. 1d). The maximum negative loadings situated over the western tropical Pacific to the eastern Indian Ocean off west Australia are in contrast to the maximum positive loadings in the southeastern tropical Pacific, establishing a typical pattern of the Walker circulation. In gross aspect, it is very similar to the oscillating behavior of El Ni\u00f1o/Southern Oscillation (ENSO) when combined with the PC time series (Philander 1989).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
